{"seq": 7, "run_id": "1189f08f20824922", "ts": "2026-09-18T00:22:15.037+00:00", "stage": "risk_manager", "event": "stage_output", "payload": {"verdict": "reject", "adjusted_stop": null, "adjusted_target": null, "adjusted_conviction": 0.1, "findings": [{"code": "no_actionable_levels", "severity": "hard", "detail": "Analyst returns no_setup with entry, stop and target all None. There is nothing to size, nothing for the limit engine to clamp, and no invalidation price to monitor. A flat read with 0.45 conviction is not a trade; it is a watchlist note, and it should not consume one of the four daily signal slots."}, {"code": "stale_price_vs_cutoff", "severity": "hard", "detail": "Price snapshot is 81 minutes old against a 90-minute actionability cutoff. The only tradeable version described (short the 4349.77-4356.04 retest) sits 5.7-12.0 points above a last-known 4344.08 \u2014 well inside one H1 ATR (18.08). That zone can have been tagged and rejected, or reclaimed outright, inside the stale window. Any level quoted from this snapshot is unverifiable by the time an order would rest."}, {"code": "direction_unresolved_pre_london", "severity": "hard", "detail": "The short case depends on London running the range low rather than the high, and the tape says the opposite of the structure: M15 swept 4340.32 and closed back above at 4344.08 (0.67 penetration, bullish rejection), while price is already inside the H1 bearish OB 4341.35-4349.77 rather than at a clean retest edge. Liquidity rests at both extremes of the 4305.05-4381.33 London range. This is a coin flip on which side gets run, dressed as a bearish continuation."}, {"code": "structural_conflict", "severity": "warning", "detail": "H4 SMC bias bullish (BOS through 4367.23) against H4 EMA trend bearish with price below EMA50 4347.29 and EMA200 4355.64; H1 SMC bearish (BOS 4351.21) against H1 structure uptrend and bullish EMA read; M15 SMC bearish against a fresh bullish sweep. Three frames disagree internally, not just with each other. No directional edge survives that."}, {"code": "hypothetical_stop_inside_noise", "severity": "warning", "detail": "A stop just above the 4356.04 OB edge from a ~4350 short entry is ~6 points \u2014 roughly 1x M15 ATR (6.24) but only 0.33x H1 ATR (18.08), below the 0.6x ATR floor, and inside a band the market has already proven it overshoots: the M15 sweep of 4355.19 closed back at 4361.88 (3.98 penetration). The 3.3 R:R on that construction is manufactured by putting the stop where price demonstrably wicks, not where the idea is wrong. The structural invalidation is above 4359.79-4365.55, which changes the geometry materially."}, {"code": "calendar_incomplete", "severity": "warning", "detail": "Calendar confidence derived_only: NFP and claims only, no FOMC/CPI/PCE dates loaded. 'No events in 72 hours' is unverified, so the 60min-before/30min-after entry blackout cannot be relied on. A short targeting 4319.52-4328.93 would need roughly a London session to fill and could be sitting through an unobserved high-impact print."}, {"code": "macro_channel_absent", "severity": "warning", "detail": "No DXY, real-yield, VIX or COT inputs supplied. The analyst is honest that no transmission channel is identifiable \u2014 correct, and it means the direction is a pure liquidity guess with no macro corroboration. Nothing here supports leaning short beyond intraday structure that is itself conflicted."}, {"code": "no_track_record", "severity": "info", "detail": "Zero journalled closed trades on this instrument/engine, so there is no evidence that Asian-session range fades or SMC OB retests convert here. First signals should be the cleanest available, not mid-range compressions."}], "commentary": "Agreed with standing aside, and I am formalising it as a reject rather than passing a levelless note downstream. There is no entry, stop or target to approve, the snapshot is 81 minutes old with 9 minutes of shelf life left, and the only trade sketched \u2014 short the 4349.77-4356.04 retest for the 4319.52-4328.93 FVG \u2014 is not on offer and would be placed blind into a zone that may already have traded. Beyond the mechanics, the idea needs London to run the low rather than the high, with resting liquidity at both extremes and a fresh M15 sweep rejection at 4340.32 arguing the other way; the attractive R:R comes from parking the stop at 4356.04, a level the tape has already overshot by 4-7 points, not at the structural invalidation above 4359.79-4365.55. Add a derived_only calendar that cannot rule out a print inside the holding period and zero macro corroboration, and this only works if nothing surprising happens. Conviction cut to 0.10. To reconsider: a price feed under 30 minutes old, an actual tag of 4351.37-4356.04 with an M15 close back under 4348.44, a stop above 4359.79 rather than at the OB lip, first target trimmed to 4328.93, and the calendar upgraded off derived_only."}, "prev_hash": "5953418e0d566edd24b36ba3a608ec6fd8f5940a3b0e0cb8149c6a87a3b81fce", "hash": "654b751e3448fdea318529698f5eb637d3b2c4ae0ebed7a90bfdb5faacb87c99"}
